{
  "$comment": "VAPP-289 (docs/round-9-contract.md §15; the spec of this file is §6): functions at A2UI 1.0, replayed by the TS reference (src/a2ui10.test.ts) and the Rust core. Inputs hand-written, `expected` from src/ by `bun run --filter @exponential_app/eui generate`; `sequences` (async) by `bun run scripts/generate-a2ui10.ts`. `coercion`: {value, expected: {boolean: coerceBoolean(value), present: present(value)}} (§6.7). `checks`: evaluateCheck(rule, data ?? {}, {catalogId: core}) → the ValidationResult (§6.6). `results`: checkResult(condition, message). `shown`: shownResult(results), the ONE result a field shows; null = all valid. `evaluations`: resolveWithFailure(value, data ?? {}, {catalogId ?? core, position ?? reactive, scope?, available?}) → {value, failure?}: failure = {code, message}, the first one (§6.8); `value` is what the position holds (null on failure). `routing`: decideRoute(input) (§6.5's table). `keys`: routedCallKey(catalogId, fn, args), RFC 8785 args. `sequences`: one host with a MemoryTransport (`agent`, `policy`, `consent`, `registered`, `data`, `sendDataModel`, `trusted` = the surface s was created by a trusted route, so it has no agent); steps in order: {read: call} = a reactive resolve (expected {value, failure?}), {press: name, args?} = await callFunction (expected FunctionOutcome), {pressAsync: name, args?} = the same, not awaited, {respond: body} = an agentFunctionResponse. `expectedSent` = every message that left in order ({message, metadata} when it has metadata), `expectedRan` = the registered functions' calls.",
